  "title": "A geometric shape regularity effect in the human brain: MEG dataset",
  "description": "Magnetoencephalography (MEG) recordings from 20 adult participants viewing simple geometric shapes such as hexagons, triangles and quadrilaterals. The dataset supports a study of how the human brain encodes geometric regularity, including symmetries and parallelism, and contrasts it with visual processing in convolutional neural networks and transformer models. It is released anonymized and defaced in BIDS format, alongside a companion fMRI dataset.",
  "methods_description": "MEG data were acquired at NeuroSpin during perception of geometric shapes. The dataset was anonymized and defaced with mne_bids (participant order shuffled, dates changed, anatomy defaced, gender information removed). Pre-processing used mne-bids-pipeline with a configuration file provided in the authors' GitHub repository.",
